\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Lower boundaries of the cod LRP kernels against the horizon $T$ under the three floors, for BAU, flat 60, 120 and 180 kt. Solid: nominal kernels of the worst-floor map (Theorem\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {thm:kernel}); dashed: exact bounded-defect kernels (Theorem\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {thm:exact}) with the declared defect $\varepsilon =329\,\mathrm  {kt}$; dotted black: Lipschitz certificate for zero catch. The grey dashed line is the LRP and the dotted line the $10\,000$-kt ceiling at which a kernel becomes empty. Under the 10th-percentile floor the nominal BAU and 60-kt kernels are the whole safe set at every horizon.}}{9}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
